text:
Alex: Quick check — I'm going to switch the `webapp` from a Deployment to a StatefulSet to stabilize the session-store PV attachments. Planning a canary-style rollout using partitioning so we only flip one pod at a time. pinging infra for any obvious gotchas.

Priya: Why StatefulSet vs keeping Deployment + leader-election + shared storage? just curious.

Alex: The session-store needs a local PV per pod (we rely on node-local storage for perf). Leader-election won't help because sticky data must live on the same node for now.

Taylor: Ok. If you go STS, make sure the terraform module changes are isolated. Our infra module currently has `kubernetes_deployment.webapp` — we should add `kubernetes_stateful_set.webapp` and keep both resources in the TF state until cutover.

Josh: Also note HPA doesn't autoscale StatefulSets directly (we use an external scaler for pods-by-label). If you expect scaling during rollout, coordinate with SRE.

Alex: here's the rough TF change I'm going to open as a PR:

```hcl
resource "kubernetes_stateful_set" "webapp" {
  metadata { name = "webapp" namespace = var.namespace }
  spec {
    replicas = var.webapp_replicas
    selector { match_labels = { app = "webapp" } }
    service_name = "webapp-headless"
    update_strategy {
      rolling_update { partition = var.rollout_partition }
      type = "RollingUpdate"
    }
    template {
      metadata { labels = { app = "webapp" } }
      spec {
        containers {
          name = "webapp"
          image = var.webapp_image
          readiness_probe { http_get { path = "/ready" port = 8080 } initial_delay_seconds = 15 timeout_seconds = 2 period_seconds = 5 }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Priya: Nice. For canary, maybe set `var.rollout_partition = 1` so 1 old pod remains, then decrement partition as we promote. Also bump `initial_delay_seconds` to 30 for the readiness probe during canary to avoid flaky failures.

Taylor: Agreed on probe bump. Also add a short-lived `preStop` hook to drain connections before termination. Example: `exec: ["/bin/sh", "-c", "/usr/local/bin/drain && sleep 5"]`.

Josh: Make sure the PDB allows at least 1 available pod during updates. If replicas=3, PDB.minAvailable should be 2. Don't block rollingUpdate with a too-strict PDB.

InfraBot: terraform plan triggered for branch `feature/sts-webapp` — plan started (will post results).

Alex: Thanks — I'll update the TF to include PDB + preStop + probe changes. Plan to do canary like: set `rollout_partition = replicas - 1`, wait for new pod to be Ready, run smoke tests, then `kubectl patch statefulset/webapp -p '{"spec":{"updateStrategy":{"rollingUpdate":{"partition":0}}}}'` to finish.

Priya: Smoke test checklist: auth login, session stickiness (write/read), and prometheus latency spike check. Share the test scripts in the PR.

Taylor: I'll review the TF PR — quick request: separate the resource move into two commits (create STS + patch services, then remove Deployment in a follow-up). Easier to rollback.

Josh: I'll stand by to handle any HPA/metrics flakiness during the window. Recommend we schedule the deploy during off-peak (US morning).

Alex: All good. I'll open the PR in ~15m and tag you @Taylor @Priya @Josh. Thanks :thumbsup:

InfraBot: terraform plan finished — no destructive changes detected for `kubernetes_stateful_set.webapp` on the feature branch.

Priya: LGTM from infra design perspective, leave the final thumbs to Taylor + Josh after PR.

Taylor: will review in the PR.

Josh: 👍 will be on-call for the deploy window.

Alex: Closing loop here once PR is merged, will post the rollout steps and smoke run outputs in this thread.
